lass=\"infobox-data\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\" style=\"margin-left:1em;text-indent:-1em;\">\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/IEEE_Emanuel_R._Piore_Award\" title=\"IEEE Emanuel R. Piore Award\">IEEE Emanuel R. Piore Award</a> (1983)<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Turing_Award\" title=\"Turing Award\">Turing Award</a> (1984)</li>\n<li><span class=\"nowrap\"><a href=\"/wiki/SIGPLAN\" title=\"SIGPLAN\">SIGPLAN</a> Programming Languages</span> Achievement Award</li>\n<li>Fellow of the <a href=\"/wiki/Computer_History_Museum\" title=\"Computer History Museum\">Computer History Museum</a> (2004)<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Marcel_Benoist_Prize\" title=\"Marcel Benoist Prize\">Marcel Benoist Prize</a> (1989)</li></ul>\n</div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><b>Scientific career</b></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Fields</th><td class=\"infobox-data category\"><a href=\"/wiki/Computer_science\" title=\"Computer science\">Computer science</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Workplaces</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\">\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/ETH_Zurich\" title=\"ETH Zurich\">ETH Zurich</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Stanford_University\" title=\"Stanford University\">Stanford University</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/University_of_Zurich\" title=\"University of Zurich\">University of Zurich</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Xerox_PARC\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Xerox PARC\">Xerox PARC</a></li></ul>\n</div></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thesis\" title=\"Thesis\">Thesis</a></th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/367593.367619\">A Generalization of Algol</a></i>&#160;<span style=\"font-size:97%;\">(1963)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\"><a href=\"/wiki/Doctoral_advisor\" title=\"Doctoral advisor\">Doctoral advisor</a></div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\"><ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Harry_Huskey\" title=\"Harry Huskey\">Harry Huskey</a></li><li><a href=\"/wiki/Edward_Feigenbaum\" title=\"Edward Feigenbaum\">Edward Feigenbaum</a></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\">Doctoral students</div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\"><ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Martin_Odersky\" title=\"Martin Odersky\">Martin Odersky</a></li><li><a href=\"/wiki/Michael_Franz\" title=\"Michael Franz\">Michael Franz</a></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr style=\"display:none\"><td colspan=\"2\">\n</td></tr><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-header\">Signature</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><span class=\"infobox-signature skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Signature_of_Niklaus_Wirth.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img alt=\"Signature of Niklaus Wirth\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Signature_of_Niklaus_Wirth.svg/250px-Signature_of_Niklaus_Wirth.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"61\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Signature_of_Niklaus_Wirth.svg/330px-Signature_of_Niklaus_Wirth.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"968\" data-file-height=\"396\" /></a></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Niklaus Emil Wirth</b> (<a href=\"/wiki/International_Phonetic_Alphabet\" title=\"International Phonetic Alphabet\">IPA</a>: <span class=\"rt-commentedText nowrap\"><span class=\"IPA nopopups noexcerpt\" lang=\"en-fonipa\"><a href=\"/wiki/Help:IPA/English\" title=\"Help:IPA/English\">/<span style=\"border-bottom:1px dotted\"><span title=\"&#39;v&#39; in &#39;vie&#39;\">v</span><span title=\"/ɛr/: &#39;err&#39; in &#39;merry&#39;\">ɛr</span><span title=\"&#39;t&#39; in &#39;tie&#39;\">t</span></span>/</a></span></span>) (15 February 1934 – 1 January 2024) was a Swiss <a href=\"/wiki/Computer_scientist\" title=\"Computer scientist\">computer scientist</a>. He designed several <a href=\"/wiki/Programming_language\" title=\"Programming language\">programming languages</a>, including <a href=\"/wiki/Pascal_(programming_language)\" title=\"Pascal (programming language)\">Pascal</a>, and pioneered several classic topics in software engineering. In 1984, he won the <a href=\"/wiki/Turing_Award\" title=\"Turing Award\">Turing Award</a>, generally recognized as the highest distinction in <a href=\"/wiki/Computer_science\" title=\"Computer science\">computer science</a>, \"for developing a sequence of innovative computer languages\".<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-ACM&#95;Turing&#95;Award&#95;4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ACM_Turing_Award-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class